===== pnpm smoke:delivery-health =====

delivery-health assessment

  ✓ a fresh lease AND a responder that answers is SERVING
  ✓ serving carries the daemon incarnation from the lease holder
  ✓ the heartbeat fact reports its real age (4000ms), not zero
  ✓ the heartbeat fact names its source as lease-kv, not the round-trip
  ✓ the affirmative fact names its source as responder-roundtrip
  ✓ the affirmative fact's own age is 0 — the daemon answered just now
  ✓ WEDGED: a ready, freshly-renewed lease with no responder REFUSES
  ✓ WEDGED: the refusal is named no-responder specifically
  ✓ WEDGED: the refusal carries the deadline it waited
  ✓ WEDGED: the refusal still reports the fresh heartbeat (1000ms) — the two facts disagree, and that IS the finding
  ✓ WEDGED: the detail names that the lease claimed ready
  ✓ WEDGED inverse control: the identical lease WITH a responder is SERVING — the responder is what decided it
  ✓ STALE: a heartbeat older than the TTL REFUSES
  ✓ STALE: the refusal is named lease-stale specifically
  ✓ STALE: the refusal carries the measured age, not just the fact of staleness
  ✓ STALE inverse control: exactly at the TTL boundary it is SERVING — age is what decided it
  ✓ NO-LEASE: an absent holder record REFUSES
  ✓ NO-LEASE: the refusal is named no-lease specifically
  ✓ NO-LEASE inverse control: the same call WITH a record is SERVING
  ✓ REFUSED: a read that throws REFUSES
  ✓ REFUSED: the refusal is named refused specifically
  ✓ REFUSED: it is NOT the no-lease refusal — a denial must never render as an absence
  ✓ REFUSED: the refusal names which read failed and why
  ✓ the state matrix is populated (guards the vacuous-every trap)
  ✓ no verdict is undefined
  ✓ every rendering names its condition and none reads as a bare unknown
  ✓ the four constructed refusal conditions are each reachable BY NAME
  ✓ and the serving arm is reachable, counted separately from the refusals
  · NOT MEASURED: `unreachable` has no producer in this suite (documented, not asserted)
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: evidence stamped in the future does not render as age 0
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: the fact reports that its age could not be established
  ✓ CLOCK-SKEW: the fact carries the measured skew, so a reader can see how far ahead
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: a lease whose writer clock is ahead REFUSES rather than passing the TTL gate
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: the machine-readable condition is clock-fault, NOT lease-stale
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: the refusal carries the measured skew on the arm itself
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW: and its detail names the direction of the fault
  ✓ CLOCK-SKEW RENDER: the operator line contains no raw null
  ✗ FAIL: CLOCK-SKEW RENDER: it names clock-fault and refuses
  ✓ CLOCK-SKEW inverse control: the same lease with a sane clock is SERVING — the skew is what decided it

